                  <tr class="oj-table">
                     <td valign="top" class="oj-table"  >
                        <p class="oj-tbl-txt">Governance</p>
                     </td>
                     <td valign="top" class="oj-table" colspan="4" >
                        <p class="oj-tbl-txt">
                           <span class="oj-bold">C9 – Gender diversity ratio in governance body</span>
                        </p>
                        <p class="oj-tbl-txt">If the undertaking has a governance body in place, the undertaking shall disclose the related gender diversity ratio.</p>
                     </td>
                     <td valign="top" class="oj-table"  >
                        <p class="oj-tbl-txt">
                           <span class="oj-bold">SFDR</span>
                           <a id="ntc40-L_202601560EN.002601-E0040" href="#ntr40-L_202601560EN.002601-E0040"
                              > (<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">40</span>)</a>
                        </p>
                        <p class="oj-tbl-txt">
                           <span class="oj-bold">Benchmark</span>
                           <a id="ntc41-L_202601560EN.002601-E0041" href="#ntr41-L_202601560EN.002601-E0041"
                              > (<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">41</span>)</a>
                        </p>
                     </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="oj-tblnote">
                     <td colspan="6" >
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr1-L_202601560EN.002601-E0001" href="#ntc1-L_202601560EN.002601-E0001"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">1</span>)</a>  This disclosure requirement is consistent with the requirements included in Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2022/2453 of 30 November 2022 amending the implementing technical standards laid down in Implementing Regulation (EU) 2021/637 as regards the disclosure of environmental, social and governance risks (<a href="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/oj/JOL_2022_324_R_TOC"
                              >OJ L 324, 19.12.2022, p. 1</a>, ELI: <a href="http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2022/2453/oj" >http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2022/2453/oj</a>) – Template 5: Banking book – Climate change physical risk: Exposures subject to physical risk.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr2-L_202601560EN.002601-E0002" href="#ntc2-L_202601560EN.002601-E0002"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">2</span>)</a>  Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288, mandatory indicator #5 in Table 1 of Annex I (‘Share of non-renewable energy consumption and production’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr3-L_202601560EN.002601-E0003" href="#ntc3-L_202601560EN.002601-E0003"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">3</span>)</a>  Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 supplementing Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 (SFDR), mandatory indicators #1 and #2 in Table 1 of Annex I (‘GHG emissions’; Carbon footprint’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr4-L_202601560EN.002601-E0004" href="#ntc4-L_202601560EN.002601-E0004"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">4</span>)</a>  Articles 5(1), 6 and 8(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/1011 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 8 June 2016 on indices used as benchmarks in financial instruments and financial contracts or to measure the performance of investment funds and amending Directives 2008/48/EC and 2014/17/EU and Regulation (EU) No 596/2014 (<a href="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/oj/JOL_2016_171_R_TOC"
                              >OJ L 171, 29.6.2016, p. 1</a>, ELI: <a href="http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/1011/oj" >http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/1011/oj</a>).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr5-L_202601560EN.002601-E0005" href="#ntc5-L_202601560EN.002601-E0005"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">5</span>)</a>  This information supports the information needs of financial market participants subject to Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 supplementing Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 (SFDR) because it is derived from (a) an additional indicator related to principal adverse impacts as set out by indicator #2 in Table 2 of Annex I to that Delegated Regulation with regard to disclosure rules on sustainable investments (‘Emissions of air pollutants’); (b) indicator #8 in Table 1 of Annex I (‘Emissions to water); (c) indicator #1 in Table 2 of Annex I (‘Emissions of inorganic pollutants’); and (d) indicator #3 in Table 2 of Annex I (‘Emissions of ozone-depleting substances’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr6-L_202601560EN.002601-E0006" href="#ntc6-L_202601560EN.002601-E0006"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">6</span>)</a>  Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 supplementing Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 (SFDR), mandatory indicator #7 in Table 1 of Annex I (‘Activities negatively affecting biodiversity-sensitive areas’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr7-L_202601560EN.002601-E0007" href="#ntc7-L_202601560EN.002601-E0007"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">7</span>)</a>  This information supports the information needs of financial market participants subject to Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 supplementing Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 (SFDR) because it is derived from a mandatory indicator related to principal adverse impacts as set out by indicator #9 in Table 1 of Annex I to that Delegated Regulation with regard to disclosure rules on sustainable investments (‘Hazardous waste and radioactive waste ratio’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr8-L_202601560EN.002601-E0008" href="#ntc8-L_202601560EN.002601-E0008"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">8</span>)</a>  This information supports the information needs of financial market participants subject to Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 supplementing Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 (SFDR), as reflecting an additional indicator related to principal adverse impacts as set out by indicator #2 in Table 3 of Annex I to that Delegated Regulation with regard to disclosure rules on sustainable investments (‘Rate of accidents’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr9-L_202601560EN.002601-E0009" href="#ntc9-L_202601560EN.002601-E0009"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">9</span>)</a>  This information supports the needs of benchmark administrators to disclose ESG factors subject to Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1816 of 17 July 2020 supplementing Regulation (EU) 2016/1011 of the European Parliament and of the Council as regards the explanation in the benchmark statement of how environmental, social and governance factors are reflected in each benchmark provided and published (<a href="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/oj/JOL_2020_406_R_TOC"
                              >OJ L 406, 3.12.2020, p. 1</a>, ELI: <a href="http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_del/2020/1816/oj" >http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_del/2020/1816/oj</a>), as set out by indicator ‘Weighted average ratio of accidents, injuries, fatalities’ in Sections 1 and 2 of Annex II to the Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1816.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr10-L_202601560EN.002601-E0010" href="#ntc10-L_202601560EN.002601-E0010"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">10</span>)</a>  Directive (EU) 2023/970 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 10 May 2023.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr11-L_202601560EN.002601-E0011" href="#ntc11-L_202601560EN.002601-E0011"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">11</span>)</a>  Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 supplementing Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 (SFDR), mandatory indicator #12 in Table 1 of Annex I (‘Unadjusted gender pay gap’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr12-L_202601560EN.002601-E0012" href="#ntc12-L_202601560EN.002601-E0012"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">12</span>)</a>  Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1816, indicator ‘Weighted average gender pay gap’ in Sections 1 and 2 of Annex II.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr13-L_202601560EN.002601-E0013" href="#ntc13-L_202601560EN.002601-E0013"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">13</span>)</a>  Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1816, indicator ‘Numbers of convictions and amount of fines for violations of anti-corruption and anti-bribery laws’ in Sections 1 and 2 of Annex II to Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1816.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr14-L_202601560EN.002601-E0014" href="#ntc14-L_202601560EN.002601-E0014"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">14</span>)</a>  This information supports the information needs of financial market participants subject to Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 supplementing Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 (SFDR), as reflecting an additional indicator related to principal adverse impacts as set out by indicator # 17 Table 3 of Annex I to that Delegated Regulation (‘Numbers of convictions and amount of fines for violations of anti-corruption and anti-bribery laws by investee companies’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr15-L_202601560EN.002601-E0015" href="#ntc15-L_202601560EN.002601-E0015"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">15</span>)</a>  Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 supplementing Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 (SFDR), mandatory indicators #1 and #2 in Table 1 of Annex I (‘GHG emissions’; Carbon footprint’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr16-L_202601560EN.002601-E0016" href="#ntc16-L_202601560EN.002601-E0016"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">16</span>)</a>  Regulation (EU) 2016/1011, Articles 5(1), 6 and 8 (1).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr17-L_202601560EN.002601-E0017" href="#ntc17-L_202601560EN.002601-E0017"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">17</span>)</a>  High climate impact sectors are those listed in NACE Sections A to H and Section M as defined in the Annex to Delegated Regulation (EU) 2023/137.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr18-L_202601560EN.002601-E0018" href="#ntc18-L_202601560EN.002601-E0018"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">18</span>)</a>  This information supports the information needs of financial market participants subject to Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 (SFDR) because it is derived from an additional indicator related to principal adverse impacts as set out by indicator #4 in Table 2 of Annex I to Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 with regard to disclosure rules on sustainable investments (‘Investments in companies without carbon emission reduction initiatives’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr19-L_202601560EN.002601-E0019" href="#ntc19-L_202601560EN.002601-E0019"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">19</span>)</a>  This information is aligned with Article 6 of Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1818 of 17 July 2020.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr20-L_202601560EN.002601-E0020" href="#ntc20-L_202601560EN.002601-E0020"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">20</span>)</a>  This information is aligned with Article 449a of Regulation (EU) No 575/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 26 June 2013 on prudential requirements for credit institutions and amending Regulation (EU) No 648/2012 (<a href="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/oj/JOL_2013_176_R_TOC"
                              >OJ L 176, 27.6.2013, p. 1</a>, ELI: <a href="http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2013/575/oj" >http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2013/575/oj</a>); Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2022/2453 of 30 November 2022 amending the implementing technical standards laid down in Implementing Regulation (EU) 2021/637 as regards the disclosure of environmental, social and governance risks (<a href="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/oj/JOL_2022_324_R_TOC"
                              >OJ L 324, 19.12.2022, p. 1</a>, ELI: <a href="http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2022/2453/oj" >http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2022/2453/oj</a>) – Template 3: Banking book – Indicators of potential climate change transition risk: alignment metrics.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr21-L_202601560EN.002601-E0021" href="#ntc21-L_202601560EN.002601-E0021"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">21</span>)</a>  This information is aligned with Article 2(1) of Regulation (EU) 2021/1119 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 30 June 2021 establishing the framework for achieving climate neutrality and amending Regulations (EC) No 401/2009 and (EU) 2018/1999 (<a href="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/oj/JOL_2021_243_R_TOC"
                              >OJ L 243, 9.7.2021, p. 1</a>, ELI: <a href="http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2021/1119/oj" >http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2021/1119/oj</a>) (‘European Climate Law’), and with Article 2 of Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1818.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr22-L_202601560EN.002601-E0022" href="#ntc22-L_202601560EN.002601-E0022"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">22</span>)</a>  Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1816 Annex II: Environmental factors to be considered by underlying assets of the benchmark.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr23-L_202601560EN.002601-E0023" href="#ntc23-L_202601560EN.002601-E0023"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">23</span>)</a>  EBA Pillar 3: ITS – Template 5: Banking book – Climate change physical risk: Exposures subject to physical risk; and EBA Pillar 3: ITS – Template 2: Banking book – Indicators of potential climate change transition risk: Loans collateralised by immovable property – Energy efficiency of the collateral.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr24-L_202601560EN.002601-E0024" href="#ntc24-L_202601560EN.002601-E0024"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">24</span>)</a>  This information supports the needs of benchmark administrators to disclose ESG factors subject to Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1816 as set out by indicator ‘Exposure of the benchmark portfolio to companies without due diligence policies on issues addressed by the fundamental International Labour Organisation Conventions 1 to 8’ in Sections 1 and 2 of Annex II to that Delegated Regulation.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr25-L_202601560EN.002601-E0025" href="#ntc25-L_202601560EN.002601-E0025"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">25</span>)</a>  This information supports the information needs of financial market participants subject to Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 because it is derived from a mandatory indicator related to principal adverse impacts as set out by indicator #11 in Table 1 of Annex I (‘Share of investments in investee companies without policies to monitor compliance with the UNGC principles or OECD Guidelines for Multinational Enterprises or grievance /complaints handling mechanisms to address violations of the UNGC principles or OECD Guidelines for Multinational Enterprises’) and by indicator #5 in Table 3 of Annex I (‘Share of investments in investee companies without any grievance/complaints handling mechanism related to employee matters’) and by indicator #9 in Table 3 of Annex I (‘Share of investments in entities without a human rights policy’) of Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 with regard to disclosure rules on sustainable investments.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr26-L_202601560EN.002601-E0026" href="#ntc26-L_202601560EN.002601-E0026"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">26</span>)</a>  This information supports the information needs of financial market participants subject to Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 because it is derived from a mandatory and additional indicator related to principal adverse impacts as set out by indicator #10 in Table 1 of Annex I and by indicator #14 in Table 3 of Annex I to Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 with regard to disclosure rules on sustainable investments (‘Violations of UNGC principles and OECD Guidelines for Multinational Enterprises’ and ‘Number of identified cases of severe human rights issues and incidents’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr27-L_202601560EN.002601-E0027" href="#ntc27-L_202601560EN.002601-E0027"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">27</span>)</a>  This information supports the information needs of benchmark administrators to disclose ESG factors subject to Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1816 as set out by indicator ‘Number of benchmark constituents subject to social violations (absolute number and relative divided by all benchmark constituents), as referred to in international treaties and conventions, United Nations principles and, where applicable, national law’ in Sections 1 and 2 of Annex II.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr28-L_202601560EN.002601-E0028" href="#ntc28-L_202601560EN.002601-E0028"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">28</span>)</a>  This information supports the information needs of financial market participants subject to Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 because it is derived from an additional indicator related to principal adverse impacts, as set out by indicator #14 in Table 1 of Annex I to Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288, and consistent with Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2025/1775.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr29-L_202601560EN.002601-E0029" href="#ntc29-L_202601560EN.002601-E0029"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">29</span>)</a>  Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1818 Article 12(1): ‘Administrators of EU-Paris aligned Benchmarks shall exclude all of the following companies from those benchmarks: companies involved in any activities related to prohibited weapons;’ and Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1816 Annex II, Sections 1, 2 and 5: ‘Weighted average percentage of benchmark constituents in the controversial weapons sector’.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr30-L_202601560EN.002601-E0030" href="#ntc30-L_202601560EN.002601-E0030"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">30</span>)</a>  This information supports the needs of benchmark administrators to disclose ESG factors subject to Regulation (EU) 2020/1818 as set out by paragraph (b) of Article 12.1.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr31-L_202601560EN.002601-E0031" href="#ntc31-L_202601560EN.002601-E0031"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">31</span>)</a>  EBA Pillar 3: Template 1: Banking book – Climate change transition risk: Companies in the manufacturing of tobacco products excluded from EU-Paris aligned Benchmarks in accordance with point (b) of Article 12(1) and in accordance with Article 12(2) of Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1818.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr32-L_202601560EN.002601-E0032" href="#ntc32-L_202601560EN.002601-E0032"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">32</span>)</a>  This information supports the needs of benchmark administrators to disclose ESG factors subject to Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1818 as set out by Article 12(1) paragraph b) of that Regulation and Section 5 of Annex II to Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1816: ‘Weighted average percentage of benchmark constituents in the tobacco sector.’</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr33-L_202601560EN.002601-E0033" href="#ntc33-L_202601560EN.002601-E0033"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">33</span>)</a>  This information supports the information needs of financial market participants subject to Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 because it is derived from an additional indicator related to principal adverse impacts set out by indicator #4 in Table 1 of Annex I to Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 with regard to disclosures rules on sustainable investments (‘Exposure to companies active in the fossil fuel sector’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr34-L_202601560EN.002601-E0034" href="#ntc34-L_202601560EN.002601-E0034"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">34</span>)</a>  This information supports the information needs of financial market participants subject to Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 because it is derived from an additional indicator related to principal adverse impacts set out by indicator #4 in Table 1 of Annex I to Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 with regard to disclosures rules on sustainable investments (‘Exposure to companies active in the fossil fuel sector’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr35-L_202601560EN.002601-E0035" href="#ntc35-L_202601560EN.002601-E0035"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">35</span>)</a>  EBA Pillar 3: Template 1: Banking book – Climate change transition risk: Companies in Mining and quarrying excluded from EU-Paris aligned Benchmarks in accordance with Article 12(1), points (d) to (g), and in accordance with Article 12(2) of Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1818.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr36-L_202601560EN.002601-E0036" href="#ntc36-L_202601560EN.002601-E0036"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">36</span>)</a>  Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1818 Article 12(1).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr37-L_202601560EN.002601-E0037" href="#ntc37-L_202601560EN.002601-E0037"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">37</span>)</a>  This information supports the information needs of financial market participants subject to Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 because it is derived from an additional indicator related to principal adverse impacts, as set out by indicator #9 in Table 2 of Annex I to Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 with regard to disclosures rules on sustainable investments (‘Investments in companies producing chemicals’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr38-L_202601560EN.002601-E0038" href="#ntc38-L_202601560EN.002601-E0038"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">38</span>)</a>  This information supports the information needs of financial market participants subject to Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 of the European Parliament and of the Council because it is derived from an additional indicator related to principal adverse impacts set out by indicator #9 in Table 2 of Annex I to Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 with regard to disclosures rules on sustainable investments (‘Investments in companies producing chemicals’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr39-L_202601560EN.002601-E0039" href="#ntc39-L_202601560EN.002601-E0039"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">39</span>)</a>  EBA Pillar 3: Template 1: Banking book – Climate change transition risk: Companies in Mining and quarrying excluded from EU-Paris aligned Benchmarks in accordance with of Article 12(1), points (d) to (g), and Article 12(2) of Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1818.</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr40-L_202601560EN.002601-E0040" href="#ntc40-L_202601560EN.002601-E0040"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">40</span>)</a>  This information supports the information needs of financial market participants subject to Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 because it is derived from an additional indicator related to principal adverse impacts set out by indicator #13 in Table 1 of Annex I to Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1288 of 6 April 2022 supplementing Regulation (EU) 2019/2088 of the European Parliament and of the Council with regard to disclosures rules on sustainable investments (‘Board gender diversity’).</p>
                        <p class="oj-note">
                           <a id="ntr41-L_202601560EN.002601-E0041" href="#ntc41-L_202601560EN.002601-E0041"
                              >(<span class="oj-super oj-note-tag">41</span>)</a>  This information supports the information needs of benchmark administrators to disclose ESG factors subject to Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/1816 as set out by indicator ‘Weighted average ratio of female to male board members’ in Sections 1 and 2 of Annex II to that Delegated Regulation.</p>
                     </td>
                  </tr>
               </tbody>
            </table>
